 did survive he was  a professional artist and he came out  and said you know I want to remember  those people who were with me in the  their sacrifice should not be in vain or  forgotten so I'm going to start doing  what I do best which is to do series of  paintings and so for the next 40 years  he painted these haunting works of in  secret from memory capturing and  recapturing those does those terrible  days of pain and suffering and death  it's an extraordinary thing that he was  able to survive and yet to capture I  think so brilliantly and hauntingly  these paintings they're on exhibit here  through December they will then were  thinking about a traveling exhibition  and then we will look for a permanent  home for this collection  hopefully in a bricks-and-mortar Museum  here in Washington DC for the victims of  communism and their memory and their  sacrifice the Cold War was something  that we fought for 45 years and I think  that as we look back upon that event  that great event we have to resolve that  never again well peoples and nations  allow so evil a tyranny to terrorize the  world  you
 

